{"parentUuid":"83b5e259-75c3-4ebf-ab72-91bbc18b4477","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"681a2a10-2b32-43fe-8600-0527272dd74e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MsMhxMjFUsok9YSAccGuyy","type":"tool_result","content":"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md:46:- A walking skeleton: one real 1850 article (the Stratford, Conn. \"knockings\" report from the first probe) goes into a scratch Atlas collection, out through an API endpoint, and onto a web page that shows the IIIF crop next to the text.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:55:- The skeleton page shows the real crop, and the crop matches its text.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:66:- The crop check on 50 random candidates spread across batches.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:77:- Kill-test evidence exists, and every crop-check failure is explained.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:143:- `export_static`, plus the cached crops for the front page and the top cases.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:14:Clipping images come straight from the Library of Congress IIIF service. Crops for the front page and the top cases are also cached as static files, so the best material survives an LoC outage.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:21:    LOC[\"LoC IIIF image service\"]\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:53:  WEB -. \"clipping crops\" .-> LOC\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:103:  - The build agent labels it before seeing any model output, from the OCR text and the scan crop where the OCR is unclear.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:154:  - `front.json`: printed-on-this-night candidates, ticker headlines and totals\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:167:- `printings[]`: article ID, LCCN, paper title, publication place, state, date, scan location, `bbox_list`, crop URLs\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:168:- `headline`, `text` (the OCR of the primary printing), `date` (earliest printing), `year`, `month_day`\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:190:- `followups[]`: each with its relation (follow-up, debunking, arrest, moved out, inquest or death notice), date, paper, quote and crop URLs\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:201:  - an Atlas Search index on headline, text, field values and town, used with fuzzy matching\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:229:scripts/                 one-off checks: keys, crop check, offline proof, numbers sheet\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:265:| LoC image service is slow or down | Lazy loading, cached crops for the top content, and a text fallback |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e59cc23f-9f34-47bc-ae43-b69b9d2631c9","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:09:44.788Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md:46:- A walking skeleton: one real 1850 article (the Stratford, Conn. \"knockings\" report from the first probe) goes into a scratch Atlas collection, out through an API endpoint, and onto a web page that shows the IIIF crop next to the text.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:55:- The skeleton page shows the real crop, and the crop matches its text.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:66:- The crop check on 50 random candidates spread across batches.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:77:- Kill-test evidence exists, and every crop-check failure is explained.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:143:- `export_static`, plus the cached crops for the front page and the top cases.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:14:Clipping images come straight from the Library of Congress IIIF service. Crops for the front page and the top cases are also cached as static files, so the best material survives an LoC outage.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:21:    LOC[\"LoC IIIF image service\"]\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:53:  WEB -. \"clipping crops\" .-> LOC\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:103:  - The build agent labels it before seeing any model output, from the OCR text and the scan crop where the OCR is unclear.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:154:  - `front.json`: printed-on-this-night candidates, ticker headlines and totals\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:167:- `printings[]`: article ID, LCCN, paper title, publication place, state, date, scan location, `bbox_list`, crop URLs\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:168:- `headline`, `text` (the OCR of the primary printing), `date` (earliest printing), `year`, `month_day`\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:190:- `followups[]`: each with its relation (follow-up, debunking, arrest, moved out, inquest or death notice), date, paper, quote and crop URLs\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:201:  - an Atlas Search index on headline, text, field values and town, used with fuzzy matching\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:229:scripts/                 one-off checks: keys, crop check, offline proof, numbers sheet\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:265:| LoC image service is slow or down | Lazy loading, cached crops for the top content, and a text fallback |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"866f7098-4c4b-4bd5-a054-fd7a3fba5bfb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-archive","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":16},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"83b5e259-75c3-4ebf-ab72-91bbc18b4477","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
