{"parentUuid":"6a56ddca-e92b-4f59-9918-3aa926f98338","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY17QvoAT1fwusBaRqjf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The verdict renders correctly. I'll update ARCHITECTURE's case model to include `display_headline` alongside `headline`, add decision 26 documenting the 2A.5 design and measurements, then run the full checks.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2128,"cache_read_input_tokens":743562,"output_tokens":3279,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1891},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2128,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3279,"cache_read_input_tokens":743562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2128},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"b995d9f3-08f1-4927-910b-590cda656404","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgY17Pqa2RenCWgapqiHd","requestRef":"d539b862-e4c1-4d6e-92b0-d6937d71f737","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c6412b5-4589-45cf-88b1-a4fb8832a063","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:10:04.687Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"4c6412b5-4589-45cf-88b1-a4fb8832a063","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY17QvoAT1fwusBaRqjf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CkxnxY2AX9US7aFhk8B9bT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\na = Path(\"Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\")\ns = a.read_text()\nold = \"- `headline`, `text` (the OCR of the primary printing), `date` (earliest printing), `year`, `month_day`\\n\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\na.write_text(s.replace(old, \"- `headline` and `text` (the OCR of the primary printing, untouched), `display_headline` (the headline without the masthead lines that lead it), `date` (earliest printing), `year`, `month_day`\\n\"))\nd = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\")\nd.write_text(d.read_text() + \"\"\"\n**26. Crops are one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline drops only the masthead lines that lead it.**\n- There is one IIIF crop per box in `bbox_list`, in its order, which is the reading order. This replaces decision 18's single crop over every box, which takes in the columns between them on a multi-column article. In 64 of 595 multi-box 1850 articles a later box starts higher on the page, so sorting boxes by height would break the order.\n- Requests to the Library of Congress:\n  - They go at most one a second, with a User-Agent that names the project.\n  - A busy answer is retried after 5 s, then 20 s. tile.loc.gov answered a region it hadn't made yet with a 503 after 35 s, and served the same URL a minute later in 0.2 s.\n  - Crops are cached under `data/crops/`, keyed by URL, and a reply that isn't an image is never cached.\n- A batch path can name a batch that LoC has since reissued. Two of the crop check's pages are recorded in `ver01` batches that tile.loc.gov no longer serves, and loc.gov lists them under `ver02`. So when a crop from a batch path is missing, loc.gov's item names the page's current service.\n- The display headline:\n  - Leading lines are dropped while they are the paper's title, its own place and state, an issue date, or a numbered volume or issue line. Lines of rules and stray marks are dropped anywhere.\n  - A weekday or month alone isn't a date line, an issue word needs a number, and a title or place under 6 letters must stand alone as a word.\n  - The stored OCR is untouched.\n- Precision, judged by hand on 200 dropped lines sampled with a fixed seed from candidate headlines (`scripts/headline_drops.py`):\n  - The first rule dropped such lines anywhere, and 142 of its 200 drops were correct (71.0%, 95% interval 64.4–76.8%). It took dates and words that belonged to the article, as in \"Out Ghosts Next / Monday Evening\".\n  - The final rule's precision is 195 of 200 (97.5%, 94.3–98.9%), and 139 of the 143 lines with letters (97.2%, 93.0–98.9%).\n  - The final rule drops 10,287 lines instead of 17,270. The cost is masthead blocks whose title line came out garbled, which now stay in the headline.\n- The crop check (`eval/results/phase2a/crop-check.md`): 48 of 50 candidates pass (96%, 95% interval 86.5–98.9%). The two failures:\n  - One page has no IIIF service: loc.gov has no item for the 1964 Arizona Tribune.\n  - One article's first box, as AmericanStories gives it, is the last line of the item above.\n\"\"\")\nPY\nmake lint >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"lint exit $?\"; uv run pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -1; .venv/bin/python -c \"from paperghosts.ingest.year import code_version; print('code_version', code_version())\"; git status --short | grep -vE '^\\?\\? data/' ","description":"Add decision 26, update ARCHITECTURE, then lint, test and list changes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2128,"cache_read_input_tokens":743562,"output_tokens":3279,"output_tokens_details":{