 at most one a second, with a User-Agent that names the project.","+  - A busy answer is retried after 5 s, then 20 s. tile.loc.gov answered a region it hadn't made yet with a 503 after 35 s, and served the same URL a minute later in 0.2 s.","+  - Crops are cached under `data/crops/`, keyed by URL, and a reply that isn't an image is never cached.","+- A batch path can name a batch that LoC has since reissued. Two of the crop check's pages are recorded in `ver01` batches that tile.loc.gov no longer serves, and loc.gov lists them under `ver02`. So when a crop from a batch path is missing, loc.gov's item names the page's current service.","+- The display headline:","+  - Leading lines are dropped while they are the paper's title, its own place and state, an issue date, or a numbered volume or issue line. Lines of rules and stray marks are dropped anywhere.","+  - A weekday or month alone isn't a date line, an issue word needs a number, and a title or place under 6 letters must stand alone as a word.","+  - The stored OCR is untouched.","+- Precision, judged by hand on 200 dropped lines sampled with a fixed seed from candidate headlines (`scripts/headline_drops.py`):","+  - The first rule dropped such lines anywhere, and 142 of its 200 drops were correct (71.0%, 95% interval 64.4–76.8%). It took dates and words that belonged to the article, as in \"Out Ghosts Next / Monday Evening\".","+  - The final rule's precision is 195 of 200 (97.5%, 94.3–98.9%), and 139 of the 143 lines with letters (97.2%, 93.0–98.9%).","+  - The final rule drops 10,287 lines instead of 17,270. The cost is masthead blocks whose title line came out garbled, which now stay in the headline.","+- The crop check (`eval/results/phase2a/crop-check.md`): 48 of 50 candidates pass (96%, 95% interval 86.5–98.9%). The two failures:","+  - One page has no IIIF service: loc.gov has no item for the 1964 Arizona Tribune.","+  - One article's first box, as AmericanStories gives it, is the last line of the item above."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b995d9f3-08f1-4927-910b-590cda656404","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-archive","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":16},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e6d300ed-3d87-4a98-94cb-aff812340f72","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
